---
description: Don't build the site for trivial changes; clean up dist after any build
alwaysApply: true
---

# No Trivial Builds

- Do NOT run `npm run build` to verify trivial changes (copy edits, class
  tweaks, single-component changes). Verify with linter diagnostics instead.
- A build is only justified before shipping (pre-push verification) or when
  a change plausibly affects the build itself (config, integrations,
  content collections schema).
- After ANY local build, delete the `dist/` folder (`rm -rf dist`); it is
  pointless to keep locally and only wastes disk space.
